    "title": "When does Justin Bieber hit the Coachella stage? How to watch live",
    "text": "April 18, 2026, 7:01 a.m. ETJustin Bieber took fans through a journey of his career during Weekend 1 of Coachella 2026.His set included selections from his recent two-part album, \"SWAG,\" as well as some oldies, including \"Beauty and a Beat,\" and \"Baby.\"The Canadian heartthrob will hopefully take fans down memory lane again for Weekend 2 when he hits the stage at the festival in Indio, California, on Saturday, April 18.Want to sing Justin Bieber's songs at the top of your lungs from your couch? Here's how to watch his upcoming Coachella performance.When is Coachella 2026?The festival is two weekends: April 10-12 and April 17-19.When is Justin Bieber headlining at Coachella 2026?Bieber headlined the festival on Saturday, April 11, and the singer will do so again on Saturday, April 18.When does Justin Bieber perform at Coachella 2026 Weekend 2?Bieber will perform on the Coachella stage on April 18 at 11:25 p.m. PDT. His set will be streaming on YouTube during that time slot.Fans can watch Coachella performances on the video platform starting April 17 at 4 p.m. PT/ 7 p.m. ET. Through the YouTube app on your TV, you can stream multiple stages simultaneously from your couch.Coachella 2026 Weekend 2 set timesA complete list of day-by-day set times can be found on Coachella's website or in an Instagram post below:Contributing: Brian Blueskye, Palm Springs Desert SunTaylor Ardrey is a news reporter for USA TODAY. You can reach her at tardrey@usatodayco.com.",
